Canonicalize installed Perl compiler configuration without changing build-time
Config modules. This is a functional seed-to-channel toolchain conversion, not
a development-file layout rule. Retain it during the recipe-local layout
migration; ordinary directory moves cannot rewrite the generated Perl lookup
semantics safely. No shared layout script is involved.

Generate separate installed Config modules from config.sh and source templates.
Keep build-time Config modules and generic installer copying unchanged.

